    given-names: Sankalp
    email: sankalp.gilda@gmail.com
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3645-4501'
repository-code: https://github.com/probityai/agent-evidence-vectors
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22758687
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22758687
    description: >-
      The concept DOI. It always resolves to the newest archived release,
      so it names the suite rather than any one revision of it.
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22803129
    description: >-
      The version DOI for 0.11.1. It names that release and never moves,
      which is what a conformance claim cites.
abstract: >-
  A recomputable execution attestation toolkit for the in-toto adversarial
  execution evidence predicate. The predicate's model is execute-and-attest
  rather than match-and-assert: a consumer recomputes the outcome from the
  bytes the statement carries instead of trusting a verdict the producer
  asserted about itself. The repository carries a second, independently usable
  implementation of that contract, so that any producer can self-certify and
  any consumer can reject a lying emitter. The corpus is versioned and
  immutable per revision: a published revision is never mutated in place, and a
  normative change regenerates every vector byte-identically from its
  generators.
keywords:
  - conformance testing
  - attestation
  - supply chain security
  - in-toto
  - provenance
  - canonicalization
  - agentic systems
  - evidence
